# Menu combo while a save dump is in progress, with the game writing its
# battery RAM continuously (churn): the 64-block dump, the pad frames, the
# overlay and the pause bit must all get through each other on the real
# serial link. The save channel shares the dpram with the game, so nothing
# pauses the dump -- the re-dirty notices churn provokes race the menu.
expect-screen "TangCore"
press down
press down
press down
press down
press b
expect-screen "game.sms"
press down
press a
expect-overlay off
expect-core smstang
wram-burst 0x000 512 0x5A
churn on
poke-save 0x10 0x42
wait-dump
hold select+start+l 500ms
expect-screen "Resume"
expect-config-bit 17 1
churn off
press a
expect-overlay off
expect-config-bit 17 0
